<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12320" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποβώμιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>far from an altar, godless,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύκλωψ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Cyc.</u>
					365
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1720.28
			</span></i>, literally, <i>not offered on an altar,</i> but on the
			ground. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>not suitable for an offering,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				5(2).403
			</span></i> (Lusi, dub.).</div>
